# 92. Why Are GPUs Useful?

Neural-network operations contain enormous amounts of parallel numerical computation.

A simplified intuition:

```text
CPU:
Small number of powerful general-purpose cores

GPU:
Large number of parallel compute units
```

Neural-network workloads can benefit enormously from parallelism.

---

# 93. Why Multiple GPUs?

Suppose a model is too large for one GPU.

We can distribute the model and/or training computation.

Simplified:

```text
Large Model
     ↓
+----+----+----+----+
↓    ↓    ↓    ↓
GPU1 GPU2 GPU3 GPU4
```

Real distributed training uses sophisticated techniques such as:

- Data parallelism
- Tensor parallelism
- Pipeline parallelism
- Distributed data parallelism
- Sharding

These will become important later.

