# 116. What Is an Embedding?

You will hear this word constantly in RAG systems.

An embedding converts an item such as text into a vector.

Conceptually:

```text
Text
 ↓
Embedding model
 ↓
[0.12, -0.42, 0.87, ...]
```

The vector represents useful semantic information.

For example:

```text
"How do I reset my password?"
```

and:

```text
"I forgot my password. How can I change it?"
```

may produce vectors that are relatively close in embedding space.

We'll study embeddings and vector databases in a later day.

