# 130. Day 4 Vocabulary

## Neural Network

A mathematical model made of connected layers of numerical transformations.

## Neuron

A basic mathematical computation unit.

## Weight

A learned numerical parameter.

## Bias

A learned numerical offset.

## Parameter

A value learned during training.

## Hyperparameter

A configuration selected by engineers.

## Forward Pass

Input flowing through the model to produce a prediction.

## Prediction

The model's current output/guess.

## Target

The correct training answer.

## Loss

A numerical measure of prediction error.

## Gradient

Information describing how loss changes with respect to parameters.

## Backpropagation

The process of calculating gradients through the network.

## Optimizer

An algorithm that uses gradients to update parameters.

## Learning Rate

Controls the size of parameter updates.

## Batch

A group of training examples processed together.

## Step

One training/update iteration.

## Epoch

Approximately one pass through the dataset.

## Pretraining

Large-scale initial model training.

